{"name":"Secret Path","hex":"#737054","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"secret","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A piece of knowledge that is hidden and intended to be kept hidden. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","The key or principle by which something is made clear; the knack."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make or keep secret.","To hide secretly."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/secret"},{"term":"path","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A trail for the use of, or worn by, pedestrians.","A course taken."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make a path in, or on (something), or for (someone).","To navigate through a file system directory tree (to a desired file or folder)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/path"}],"entries":[{"title":"Secret Path","blocks":[{"text":"Secret Path is a Canadian multimedia storytelling project including a ten-song music album, a graphic novel, an animated television film, and instructional materials. Released on October 18, 2016, the centrepiece of the project is a concept album about Chanie Wenjack, a young Anishinaabe boy from the Marten Falls First Nation who died in 1966 while trying to return home after escaping from an Indian residential school."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/bd/Secret_Path_cover_art.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Secret_Path"},{"title":"Secrecy","blocks":[{"text":"Secrecy is the practice of hiding information from certain individuals or groups who do not have the \"need to know\", perhaps while sharing it with other individuals. That which is kept hidden is known as the secret."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/If_you_talk_too_much%2C_this_man_may_die.jpg/330px-If_you_talk_too_much%2C_this_man_may_die.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thum